<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Mu'azzam Isa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1176">1176</a>–<a href="/years/1227">1227</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">al-Mu'azzam Isa was the Ayyubid ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> from 1218 to 1227, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-adil">al-Adil</a> and nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fifth-crusade">Fifth Crusade</a> he had the walls of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> dismantled in 1219 so that the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusaders</a> could not hold it. He quarrelled with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-kamil">al-Kamil</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and was a noted scholar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanafi-school">Hanafi</a> law.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-muazzam-isa.jpg" alt="al-Mu'azzam Isa" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yaakov Shoham · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dome_temple-mount_ws.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
